      {
        "id": 248871,
        "name": "",
        "username": "Omegatron",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/omegatron/{size}/4904_2.png",
        "created_at": "2022-10-23T20:59:26.906Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"El_Nate\" data-post=\"3\" data-topic=\"29707\" data-full=\"true\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/35a633/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> El_Nate:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Wow. What was your general strategy?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I just focused on hitting the limbs, which I know sounds unhelpfully obvious.</p>\n<p>Legacy focused on damage buffing, when he got the ring he spent most of the game using his base power and Motivational Charge. I did draw Next Evolution and Lead From The Front but I think playing them would have slowed the heroes down too much.</p>\n<p>Haka used Rampage to clear out the limbs whenever Akash played Primeval Eruption and otherwise spent most of the game hitting them with Taiaha.</p>\n<p>Bunker spent most of the game using Turret Mode, Flak Cannon, and Grenade Launcher.</p>\n<p><s>Arboreal Phalanges</s> Ensnaring Brambles were the priority limb to get rid of when they were out so we could all keep dealing damage. Part way through the game, the environment played Fiery Crystalization, at which point I made sure to get rid of any magmarians that came out to avoid losing equipment. When Entomb was played I just let it hit everyone, because we had no other way to get rid of it.</p>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2022-10-24T08:53:26.370Z",
        "reply_count": 1,
        "reply_to_post_number": 3,
